  <static seed="1948" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/RadicalsAndRationalExponents/RationalizeDenominator10.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\frac{7}{\sqrt{{81}}}}</m>  =   <fillin characters="9" name="AnSwEr0001"/> .</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{7}{9}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Because the denominator in this problem is a perfect square, we can easily evaluate the square root:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{7}{\sqrt{{81}}} = \frac{7}{9} }</m></p>
</solution>
